  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreComm 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'After seeing promising results in animal studies, a research team begins
    planning a clinical trial for a new treatment approach. You ask how they will
    design the trial so people from diverse communities can take part.


    How
    could this question influence study design?'
  explanation: By raising this question, the community advocate encourages the research
    team to think about who can realistically join the trial and how to reduce barriers
    to participation. Asking this at the preclinical stage helps guide the trial
    design from the beginning. This helps ensure the study includes diverse perspectives
    so the results better reflect the real-world community the treatment is meant
    to serve.
  correctAnswer: It encourages the team to plan recruitment and access strategies
    that include diverse communities
  incorrectAnswer1: It could change how the new treatment is tested in the lab
  incorrectAnswer2: It could determine the treatment dose that will be used during
    the trial
  incorrectAnswer3: It helps the team decide which patients and how many will receive
    the trial treatment
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: PreClinical
